From 40f559a0e298bb6eaa65f6a5e9072675bb5ca87e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:54:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] perf(moe): masked slice-partial top-k sum without dead-route
 clearing

With slice partials the deterministic fused kernel cleared the six
partial rows of every pair routed to no local expert, and the fixed-order
top-k sum read all num_topk * slices rows per token, dead ones included.
Dead verification rows arrive as such pairs, so at eight streams the
clearing and the reads grow with speculative work that never counts.

The top-k sum now takes the route ids for slice partials, reads each
(token, route) expert id once and skips the rows of routes outside
[0, num_experts), summing live rows in the same route-then-slice order
eight columns per thread with 16-byte accesses; the kernel no longer
clears those rows. Results match the previous order bitwise (a skipped
row was an added +0.0). The mask and slice count join the top-k sum's
compile key only when set.
